    <item>
      <title>Towards population-specific brain charts across the lifespan</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-026-02596-0</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Human Behaviour, Published online: 23 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-026-02596-0"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41562-026-02596-0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;A study of the largest available Chinese lifespan-wide structural neuroimaging dataset (comprising 43,037 participants aged 0–100 years) established population-specific brain charts, revealing developmental trajectories that diverge from those of predominantly white populations. These tailored charts improved typical phenotypic prediction and better captured disease-related deviations, advancing equitable precision neuroscience.</content:encoded>
      <dc:title>Towards population-specific brain charts across the lifespan</dc:title>
      <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41562-026-02596-0</dc:identifier>
